## Original Content
It has now been three years since the Japanese government began to discharge contaminated wastewater from the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power station into the Pacific Ocean despite strong opposition and concerns at home and abroad.

## Summary
The article marks the three-year anniversary of Japan's discharge of contaminated wastewater from the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant into the Pacific Ocean, despite ongoing opposition and concerns at home and abroad. It highlights continued environmental and health worries associated with the radioactive contamination.

## Key Points
- The discharge of contaminated wastewater from Fukushima Daiichi began three years ago.
- Japan is releasing the wastewater into the Pacific Ocean.
- There is strong domestic and international opposition to the discharge.
- The wastewater is contaminated, raising concerns about radiation and environmental impact.
- The event underscores the prolonged challenges in nuclear disaster management.


